  "rationale": "The workflow runs on push and pull_request triggers. When multiple commits are pushed to the same branch or PR in quick succession, only the latest run is needed. The P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE pattern supports canceling superseded runs to save CI resources while preserving run identity and audit records. Adding a concurrency group partitioned by workflow and ref (branch/PR) isolates different branches and PRs, so canceling only affects superseded runs of the same check. The latest run still completes, preserving all build and test coverage. This is a minimal change with no new privileged actions, secrets, publishing/deployment operations, or new network access.",
